@about
new-page: true

= About v0.2

This public demo begins in January 1949 from the viewpoint of the
opposition. It does not treat the opposition as a single
organization:
{!<span class="term term-mossadegh">!}Mohammad Mossadegh{!</span>!}, the
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!}, and
other constitutional politicians retain distinct positions. The campaign
covers the
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}National Front{!</span>!}'s
formation, the disputed Sixteenth
{!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!}, and the passage of
the nationalization principle through the
{!<span class="term term-senate">!}Senate{!</span>!} on
20 March 1951. It begins before the constitutional emergency created by the
February attempt on the
{!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Shah{!</span>!} and ends when the
nationalization principle has passed both chambers. Premiership and the later
struggle over implementation lie beyond this release.

